  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map` again, and all tests pass.\n\n**Cause:** when a subcommand's context was created, it was given the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the nested entry under its own name. The one-line fix is in `src/click/core.py:392`: `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. When there is no entry for that subcommand, this gives `None`, which existing code already handles.\n\n**Also changed:**\n- **Test:** `test_default_map_subcommands` in `tests/test_defaults.py` covers a direct subcommand, a subcommand inside a nested group, and falling back to the option's own default when the subcommand has no entry. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- **Changelog:** there's an entry in `CHANGES.md` (the plan said `CHANGES.rst`, but the repo uses Markdown). Because 8.5.0 is already released, I put it under a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2013 Unreleased\" heading; rename that if you want a different version.\n\nFull suite: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. Nothing is committed yet.",
